WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.434
-Entertainment news --
we're just one month away

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.901
from the release of
Taylor Swift's

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.734
10th studio album,
"Midnights."

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:08.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.067
And fans are already finding
all kinds of secret messages

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:14.133
about the album in
her social media posts.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.968
-Oh, man. All that stuff is just
conspiracy theories, though.

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.601
-Uh, I don't know, Tariq,
the clues are --

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.200
the clues are everywhere.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.834
-What clues?

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:24.534
-Okay, so Taylor made a surprise
announcement at this year's VMAs

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.801
that her 10th studio album was
gonna be called "Midnights,"

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:29.434
and it would come out on
midnight on October 21st.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.167
You follow?
-Uh --

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.868
-So, 13 is Taylor's favorite
number, and "Midnights"

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:35.467
is gonna have 13 tracks on it,

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.133
but nobody knows what the songs
are called yet.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.934
On all the album art
she's shared so far,

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.767
all the songs have fake titles
like "Track One,"

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.467
"Track two,"
that kind of thing.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.601
-And that means?

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.734
-But, when she posted a video
announcing

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.133
all the limited edition vinyls,
the names of the songs

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.667
were all blurred out on
the covers,

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.167
so you can tell the songs
won't actually be called

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.067
"Track One," "Track Two."

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.300
And that was on September 1st.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.701
Then on September 16th,
she posted another video,

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.968
revealing that if you line up
the backs of all

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.701
the special edition vinyls
with the regular edition ones,

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.000
it makes a clock.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.033
Midnight is a time on a clock.

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:07.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.934
-Okay. Okay, well, I guess --
-Yeah, but here --

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:10.968
here's where it gets
interesting.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.634
In Taylor's entire discography,

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:16.067
she's only sung the word
"midnight" in six songs.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.033
She sings it in "Style"
off of "1989,"

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.968
"You Are in Love" off of "1989,"
"New Year's Day"

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:21.100
off of "Reputation,"

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.567
"The Last Great American
Dynasty" off "Folklore,"

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.334
"Happiness" off of "Evermore,"
and of course,

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.534
in "22 (Taylor's version)"
of "Red (Taylor's version)."

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.067
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:30.167
And that's not even
the crazy part.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.834
'Cause it also turns out
she's sung the phrase

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:33.400
"middle of the night,"
in seven songs

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.634
throughout her discography.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.534
She sings it in "Ready For It?"
off "Reputation,"

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:37.667
"Daylight" off of "Lover,"

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:38.834
"You Belong With Me
(Taylor's version)"

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.300
off of
"Fearless (Taylor's version),"

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.400
"Untouchable
(Taylor's version),"

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.801
off of
"Fearless (Taylor's version),"

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.667
"All Too Well (10 minute
version) (Taylor's version)"

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.267
off of "Red (Taylor's version),"

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.400
"Better man (Taylor's version)"
off of "Red (Taylor's version),"

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.601
and in "Nothing New
(feat. Phoebe Bridgers)

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.534
(Taylor's version)" off of
"Red (Taylor's version)."

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:56.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.033
-What are you even saying?

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:01.167
-Six "midnights" plus seven
"middle of the nights"

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.567
equal 13.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.501
13 is Taylor's favorite number.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.367
That's how many songs
are on "Midnights!"

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.567
Taylor's a genius!

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:09.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.067
♪♪

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:14.634
That's what I was getting at.
You get it now?

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.200
-Yeah, I get it.
Happy birthday.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.968
-Thank you.
-[ Laughs ]

